#: manual/architecture_rfc.md:1
msgid "RFC 0001: Luna-Flow numerical calculus foundation architecture"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture_rfc.md:3
msgid "Status: experimental validation"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture_rfc.md:4
msgid "Target version: next major version"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture_rfc.md:5
msgid "Scope: architecture, algorithm selection and API feasibility; does not replace the current production implementation"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture_rfc.md:7
msgid "1. Decision summary"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture_rfc.md:9
msgid "The next-generation `calculus-numerical` no longer takes GSL's `Double` API and implementation structure as its blueprint. Instead, it is built on Luna-Flow's algebraic traits, checked arithmetic and explicit numerical contexts."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture_rfc.md:11
msgid "When the migration is carried out, the current `basic`, `deriv`, `diff` and `integration` APIs move into `legacy/*` and keep a compatibility period of one major version."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture_rfc.md:12
msgid "In its first phase the new API supports only same-type scalar functions `(T) -> T`. The coordinate type, the return type and the error scalar are not separated for now."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture_rfc.md:13
msgid "`Double` and `Float` use fast context-free implementations; `Decimal` and `BinFloat` use explicit context adapters."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture_rfc.md:14
msgid "Full entry points must take a context, tolerances and resource limits; convenience entry points may use a documented default context. The default for Decimal is Decimal128."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture_rfc.md:15
msgid "Numerical algorithms return named results and diagnostics instead of tuples whose meaning is opaque."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture_rfc.md:16
msgid "`estimated_error` denotes an empirical error estimate. Only implementations based on interval arithmetic or BallFloat may return a `certified_bound`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture_rfc.md:18
msgid "2. Standards and independent implementation"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture_rfc.md:20
msgid "2.1 Numerical semantics"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture_rfc.md:22
msgid "Classification, rounding and special values of binary and decimal floating point follow IEEE 754-2019."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture_rfc.md:23
msgid "Decimal context, flags, cohort and exception semantics follow the General Decimal Arithmetic specification and the decNumber test specification."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture_rfc.md:24
msgid "Arbitrary-precision reference values are generated with MPFR or Arb; no particular machine `Double` implementation is taken as the standard of correctness."
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture_rfc.md:26
msgid "2.2 Algorithm sources"
msgstr ""

#: manual/architecture_rfc.md:28
msgid "Implementations are based on papers and published algorithm descriptions; mature libraries are consulted only to cross-check interfaces and behavior:"
